-- title:
--   From HTo G G Hat Sandwich Family Cons Outcome
-- statement:
--   **The G-hat sandwich family has the expected cons outcome.** Let the parameters have a field model, let $F$ be the indexed polynomial family, let $n$ be a natural number, let $x\in\mathbb{F}_q$, and let $\mathbf x$ be a point tuple of length $n$. For a completed head outcome $g$ and tail outcome tuple $h$, write $U$ for the indexed head effect and $T$ for the tail half-product operator specified by the formal statement. If $\mathcal S$ denotes the corresponding G-hat sandwich family, then
--
--   $$
--   \mathcal S(\operatorname{cons}(x,\mathbf x),\operatorname{cons}(g,h))=UTT^\dagger U.
--   $$
--
--   The identity exposes the head indexed measurement on both sides of the tail half-product and supplies the operator formula used by the cons type-sum and tail-stage identities.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.fromHToG_gHatSandwichFamily_cons_outcome`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
